<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD JATS (Z39.96) Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v1.0 20120330//EN" "JATS-archivearticle1.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">J Cell Biol</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="hwp">jcb</journal-id><journal-title-group><journal-title>The Journal of Cell Biology</journal-title></journal-title-group><issn pub-type="ppub">0021-9525</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1540-8140</issn><publisher><publisher-name>The Rockefeller University Press</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2654134</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">20070401020090120c</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1083/jcb.20070401020090120c</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject><subj-group><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Sequential roles for myosin-X in BMP6-dependent filopodial extension, migration, and activation of BMP receptors</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Pi</surname><given-names>Xinchun</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Ren</surname><given-names>Rongqin</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Kelley</surname><given-names>Russell</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Chunlian</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Moser</surname><given-names>Martin</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Bohil</surname><given-names>Aparna B.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>DiVito</surname><given-names>Melinda</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Cheney</surname><given-names>Richard E.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Patterson</surname><given-names>Cam</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>23</day><month>2</month><year>2009</year></pub-date><volume>184</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>611</fpage><lpage>611</lpage><permissions><copyright-year>2009</copyright-year></permissions></article-meta></front><body><p>Vol. 179 No. 7, December 31, 2007. Pages <related-article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="179" page="1569" id="d31e106" xlink:href="18158328" ext-link-type="pubmed">1569&#x02013;1582</related-article>.</p><p>The siRNA sequence information of myosin-X listed in the Materials and methods is incorrect. A corrected sequence is provided below. The authors apologize for this oversight.</p><p>Myo10 siRNA1 primers (5&#x02032;-GATCCGCCAGACGAGAAGATATTTATTCAAGAGATAAATATCTTCTCGTCTGGCTTTTTTAAGCTTG-3&#x02032; and 5&#x02032;-AATTCAAGCTTAAAAAAGCCAGACGAGAAGATATTTATCTCTTGAATAAATATCTTCTCGTCTGGCG-3&#x02032;) and siRNA2 primers (5&#x02032;-GATCCGGCAATGCGAAGACAGTATATTCAAGAGATATACTGTCTTCGCATTGCCTTTTTTAAGCTTG-3&#x02032; and 5&#x02032;-AATTCAAGCTTAAAAAAGGCAATGCGAAGACAGTATATCTCTTGAATATACTGTCTTCGCATTGCCG-3&#x02032;) were used for synthesis of double-stranded DNA (Invitrogen).</p></body></article>